nfidence": null}, {"t_ms": 54268, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01MW6W8cKd8iLRzMsa4anEWq", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54268, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01MW6W8cKd8iLRzMsa4anEWq", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55811, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0147ZLhio5meT9eBL6e8zgxK", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56111, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0147ZLhio5meT9eBL6e8zgxK", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56111, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0147ZLhio5meT9eBL6e8zgxK", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60205, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and passing health checks. The error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%. SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open, which pages the on-call engineer.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy. v2.3.1 and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) were both unhealthy. The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system, which left us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I retried once and it finished in all regions.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had already been created, so there's only one. The incident describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry) and two follow-ups: finding the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and looking into the error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XtWdf9oJcf7kTc1zAMgjs6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Psi3eK2uhaVgGrD4RL6Qpx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_014JwhPuQw3qDLGqAoufQW1e", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019pXKDnVjVtwHuq4669crc6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to v2.3.0 is safe to repeat, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CyJG2jRQELrQLBKs28kH2H", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TUNSGYHs6xewsntpAeXfwy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012VwyBYeucxvArxHZ7FPmuz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MW6W8cKd8iLRzMsa4anEWq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both marked unhealthy in the deploy history. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error. That left the regions on different versions: us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. A retry finished the rollback. All regions now run v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_0147ZLhio5meT9eBL6e8zgxK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and passing health checks. The error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%. SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open, which pages the on-call engineer.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy. v2.3.1 and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) were both unhealthy. The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system, which left us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I retried once and it finished in all regions.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had already been created, so there's only one. The incident describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry) and two follow-ups: finding the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and looking into the error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}